Package: lindos-desktop
Version: 1.0.0
Section: x11
Priority: optional
Architecture: all
Maintainer: Lindos Team <team@lindos.dev>
Depends: xfce4-panel, xfce4-whiskermenu-plugin, xfwm4, xfconf, xfce4-settings, xfce4-notifyd, picom, xfce4-panel-profiles, xfce4-clipman-plugin, xfce4-screenshooter, xfce4-taskmanager, lightdm, slick-greeter, plymouth, fontconfig, lindos-core, python3
Recommends: xfce4-docklike-plugin, xfce4-pulseaudio-plugin, xfce4-power-manager, network-manager-gnome, librsvg2-bin, fonts-noto-color-emoji, fonts-noto-core, xfce4-appfinder, thunar, xfdesktop4, xfce4-session, xfce4-terminal, mintinstall, mousepad, ristretto, evince, vlc, policykit-1-gnome | mate-polkit | lxpolkit
Suggests: lindos-settings, lindos-setup, fonts-jetbrains-mono, emote
Homepage: https://lindos.dev
Description: Lindos desktop look and feel (Windows-11-style XFCE)
 Default XFCE configuration for Lindos: a 48 px bottom taskbar with a
 centred Start button and pinned apps (Whisker Menu + Docklike), a dark
 translucent panel, a two-line clock, Windows-style keyboard shortcuts
 (Super+E, Super+I, Super+L, Super+X, Super+Shift+S, ...), xfwm4 and
 xsettings defaults (Lindos-Dark GTK theme, Lindos icons, Lindos cursors,
 Selawik UI font), picom compositor profile with the lindos-compositor
 helper, GTK CSS overlay, five original SVG wallpapers, Plymouth boot
 theme, LightDM/slick-greeter branding, per-mode panel layouts for the
 five Lindos Modes (Everyday, Gaming, Work, Creator, Lite), the
 File Explorer / Settings / Store / Terminal launcher shims, and the
 autostart entry that starts lindos-core's read-only update-notifier on
 login (lindos-update-notify.sh; SPEC-UPDATE.md §37) and one that starts a
 graphical polkit authentication agent (polkit-agent-start.sh: whichever of
 policykit-1-gnome, mate-polkit or lxpolkit is installed), so the
 administrator-password prompt is a normal dialog instead of a text prompt.
 A further autostart entry (lindos-live-session) acts in the live USB session
 only and turns off sleep, screen blanking, lock and lid-suspend there, so a
 long installation is never interrupted; installed sessions are untouched.
 Another one (lindos-browser-default) runs 'lindos-browser sync-default' at
 login: when Chrome was still to be downloaded while Lindos Setup ran, it makes
 Chrome XFCE's preferred web browser once the silent retry has installed it
 (the base system's own default says Firefox) - never over a browser the user
 picked, and never in the live session.
 .
 It also keeps the base system's own branding from showing through: the
 base's Welcome Screen and Software Manager menu entries (duplicates of
 Lindos Setup and Lindos Store), its file-sharing, notes, backup and USB
 tools and the Xfce/Thunar settings entries are hidden, the update and driver
 tools get Lindos names and icons, the base's theme packs are hidden from the
 pickers, and the display names in /etc/lsb-release, /etc/linuxmint/info and
 the GRUB menu say Lindos - re-applied after every apt run (rebrand-base.py,
 /etc/apt/apt.conf.d/99lindos-branding). The base's artwork defaults no longer
 outrank Lindos's (/etc/xdg/xdg-xfce is diverted and replaced), its boot-time
 rewrite of Firefox's distribution.ini is switched off, and Lindos's default
 applications (Mousepad, Ristretto, Evince, VLC) are registered in
 /etc/xdg/mimeapps.list. Identity fields the base's tools rely on (ID,
 DISTRIB_ID, codenames) are left alone.
 .
 The GTK/icon/cursor themes themselves (built from Fluent by
 build/fetch-assets.sh) and the Selawik/Inter fonts are installed by the
 ISO build; this package never downloads anything at install time.
 .
 xfce4-docklike-plugin is a Recommends, not a Depends: as of this writing it
 is not packaged for Ubuntu 24.04 "noble" (only Ubuntu 25.10+ and Debian
 trixie+ carry it) — see docs/BUILDING.md. The panel layouts ship with it in
 slot plugin-2; without it the taskbar uses xfce4-panel's own task list and
 one launcher per installed pinned app instead (taskbar-fallback.py, applied
 at the first login and when the mode panel profiles are built), so a
 fresh session always has a window list. That variant is left-aligned,
 because the task list fills the bar.
